The evidence is consistent enough to conclude. Kubelet events show reservation's pod in a crash loop (Killing, Pulled, Created, Failed, BackOff), its restart counter climbs from 1 to 6, and its container is not ready, while frontend's calls to it fail immediately.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "reservation",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, count(*) n, min(value) mn, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name ILIKE 'reservation-%' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.restarts','k8s.container.ready') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Reservation pod restarts rose to 3-6 (normal 1) and container ready is 0 throughout the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, attr_k8s_deployment_name, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.deployment.available' AND attr_k8s_deployment_name='reservation' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Reservation deployment availability is 0 from about 21:35 onward and never recovers in the window."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT regexp_extract(message,'\"reason\":\"([A-Za-z]+)\"',1) reason, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='' AND message ILIKE '%reservation-7dfb857f97-txs78%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Kubelet events for the reservation pod show Killing, Pulled, Created, Failed and BackOff, a crash loop."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='reservation'", "claim": "Reservation emits no spans in the abnormal window, versus about 700 internal and 355 server spans normally."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "reservation", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [
       {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6 med_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='reservation.Reservation/CheckAvailability' AND service_name='frontend' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend's CheckAvailability calls to reservation fail with Error status, about 1158 of 1160, in about 0.015 ms."},
       {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend's /hotels server spans return HTTP 500 Error for 1158 of 1160 requests."}
     ]}
  ]
}
```

